nore the 304  and now we want to find the closest cube  without going over  so 39 is between 27 and 64.  so it's actually closest to 27 without  going over which means it's closest to  the cube of three  and that gives us the other part of our  answer which is three  so here we have it we put the numbers  together and 34 is the cube root of 39  304  [Music]  so why would this ever be useful so  here's a trick you can do  ask someone to pick a number from one to  a hundred and just think about it  secretly don't have them tell you the  number  have them cube the number on a  calculator  and ha once they cube the number they  tell you the cube and you instantly can  tell them the cube root by using this  table and using the trick  so let's imagine they tell you the  number is  636 056  so we look at the last digit which is  six  and when the last digit is six that  corresponds to the number six  and then we look at the we ignored the  last three digits and we look at 636  that's between the cubes of eight and  nine so we put eight  and therefore the cube root is  eighty-six  so once you get use once you've  memorized this table it'll actually be  able to do this very quickly let's do  another example  185  193  we look at the last digit of three  that corresponds to the number seven  because three and seven flip  then we ignore the last three digits and  we look at 185  and that's closest to the cube of five  without going over  so that gives us the answer of 57  so it's a pretty neat trick  and if you want to know how this works  you can click through i've made a short  video which gives the math crew  if you like this video please subscribe  to my channel  you can support me on patreon to get  exclusive rewards catch me on my blog  mind your decisions on twitter at  preshellwalker and you can get my books  listed on my website
 

